 # 3D Texture Proxy Geometry
 
-Also called: 3D Texture Mapping, 3D Texture Proxy, 3D Texture-Based Volume Rendering, View-port aligned slice projection, nVidia texture shader extension
+Also called: 3D Texture Proxy, 3D Texture-Based Volume Rendering, VR Basado en Texturas 3D, VR con texturas tridimensionales, texturas 3D con planos orientados al plano de proyección
 
 ## Overview
-3D Texture Proxy Geometry is a GPU-accelerated volume rendering technique where the volumetric dataset is uploaded as a 3D texture object, and polygonal slices parallel to the viewpoint are rasterized and blended back-to-front to form the final image [S1, S2, unofficial]. It differs from ray casting by using hardware-accelerated texture sampling and interpolation rather than explicit ray marching, and from 2D texture mapping by supporting arbitrary viewing orientations without pre-computing multiple 2D slices [S3, unofficial]. Unlike ray casting, it cannot skip unseen voxels, rendering all voxels within the view frustum [S1, unofficial].
+3D Texture Proxy Geometry is a GPU-accelerated volume rendering technique where the volumetric dataset is uploaded as a 3D texture object, and polygonal slices are rasterized and blended back-to-front to form the final image [S1, S2, unofficial]. It differs from ray casting by relying on hardware-accelerated texture sampling and interpolation rather than explicit ray marching, and from 2D texture mapping by using a single 3D texture to eliminate popping artifacts and support arbitrary viewing orientations without pre-computing multiple 2D slices [S3, S5, unofficial]. Unlike ray casting, it cannot skip unseen voxels, rendering all voxels within the view frustum [S1, unofficial].
 
